  "provenance": {
    "pattern": "uplifting trance: a four-bar anthem line on a bright sawtooth lead — long notes climbing to the fifth and falling back through the scale — over four on the floor and the offbeat bass",
    "knowledge": "public knowledge of the genre: the pattern as drummers, producers and tutorials commonly write it; no recording was sampled, transcribed from audio or mined",
    "note": "Four bars of lead: a dotted climb (root, third, fifth) held over the bar, a step past it and down through the scale to rest on the third — the shape of a trance hook, not any one tune. The lead is the stacked, detuned supersaw — in this kitchen an ensemble (a pad) and not a keyboard, because the sustained player draws only bed-capable voices and the saw lead is declared a keyboard that does not sustain as a bed. With the offbeat bass under it."
  }
